---
import { ExternalLink } from "@/components/external-link"
import Prose from "@/layouts/prose.astro"
---

<Prose title="Privacy" description="How News Shuffle uses browser data.">
  <p>
    News Shuffle stores your shuffle filters and theme in this browser. You can
    remove them by clearing this site’s data in your browser settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your browser requests source icons from Google, using each source’s
    hostname. Google receives the request and its connection details. See{" "}
    <ExternalLink href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">
      Google’s privacy policy
    </ExternalLink>
    .
  </p>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics to measure page visits and use of the Open button.
    Google can receive cookieless measurements while consent is denied. Shuffle
    events contain neither your filters nor the source you opened.
  </p>
  <p>
    Google and its advertising partners may use cookies to serve ads based on
    previous visits to this or other sites, subject to your privacy choices. If
    you see a consent message, use Privacy and cookie settings at the bottom of
    each page to change or withdraw your choice. Learn{" "}
    <ExternalLink href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">
      how Google uses data from partner sites
    </ExternalLink>{" "}
    or adjust personalised ads in{" "}
    <ExternalLink href="https://adssettings.google.com/">
      Google Ads Settings
    </ExternalLink>
    .
  </p>
  <p>
    When you open a source, that website handles your visit under its own
    privacy practices.
  </p>
  <p>
    For questions, email{" "}
    <a href="mailto:privacy@mickschroeder.com">privacy@mickschroeder.com</a>.
  </p>
</Prose>
